@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using BankPromptKind = SpaceSails.Client.Pages.Map.BankPromptKind
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE BANK PROMPT, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* #948 · THE PAGE, BEFORE THE BANK. Owner: "I would like to save this point with a comment field and a
       captain's name of my whim. I want this moment, not that I die and that situation overwrites this."

       Banking was one silent click into a berth that then read like every other berth. It now stops for the
       two lines that make a save findable a month later — a TITLE, offered pre-filled as
       "<captain> — <place> — day N" so accepting the default costs one keystroke, and a NOTE about what you
       were doing. The one sheet serves three gestures because all three write the same page: bank into a
       berth, export a file (the file carries the page with it), and rewrite the page of a bank already on
       the shelf. The second half of the owner's sentence needs no code: a banked berth was never touched by
       the autosave (#310's law, pinned by a Core guard in this lane) — the sheet says so out loud. *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="start-picker-backdrop">
            @* #997 wave 6 · THE TWO SHEETS OF THIS FAMILY THAT REALLY ARE DECISIONS — this one and the
               import consent below. They are the only two of the four `.start-picker` surfaces that any of
               the shell's three shapes fits; the front door and the logbook are named as stragglers at their
               own root above, with the reason.

               `ByDecision` is the critical-decision exception: no ✕, because every answer the surface offers
               is itself a close. That is true here, and it is proved by PRESSING rather than taken from this
               comment (TheShellOwnsTheStartPickerFamilyTests) — CommitBankPrompt runs CancelBankPrompt before
               it writes anything, and CancelBankPrompt clears _bankPrompt and nothing else, so both roads end
               the sheet. The title and the note are FIELDS, not answers, and a field is not a way out.

               The two answers stay the page's own markup inside `.save-surface-foot-center` rather than going
               through the shell's `Choices`, for #1001's reason: they wear different colours (btn-success on
               the commit, btn-outline-light on the cancel) and the commit changes its face with the kind of
               sheet this is, while `ChoiceClass` is one class list for all of them. Routing them would
               repaint two buttons, and this migration does not move a pixel.

               `Bare` because the sheet has no head row to give up — `.start-picker-title` is the page's own
               centred div with the page's own rule — and because `Hosted`'s `display: contents` would put a
               wrapper between this root and `.save-surface-foot`.

               No `StopClicks`: this backdrop carries no @@onclick, so there is nothing behind the sheet for a
               click on it to fall through to. *@
            <OverlayShell class="start-picker save-surface bank-sheet"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.ByDecision">
                <div class="start-picker-title">@BankPromptHeading</div>
                <div class="start-picker-sub">
                    @(bankKind == BankPromptKind.Edit
                        ? "Rewrite this berth's page. The saved voyage inside it is not touched, and it does not move in the list."
                        : "Give this moment a name you will recognise, and a note about what you were doing. Both travel with the save.")
                </div>
                <label class="bank-field">
                    <span class="bank-field-label">Title</span>
                    <input class="bank-input" maxlength="@SaveSlotLabels.MaxTitleLength" autofocus
                           placeholder="A title of your whim"
                           value="@_bankTitle" @oninput="e => _bankTitle = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty" />
                </label>
                <label class="bank-field">
                    <span class="bank-field-label">Note — what were you doing?</span>
                    <textarea class="bank-input bank-note" rows="4" maxlength="@SaveSlotLabels.MaxNoteLength"
                              placeholder="Heading for the ice with a full hold and one collector three days behind."
                              value="@_bankNote" @oninput="e => _bankNote = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty"></textarea>
                </label>
                @if (bankKind != BankPromptKind.Export && _bankSlotId != SaveSlotBook.AutoSlotId)
                {
                    <div class="bank-safety">🔒 A banked berth is never overwritten by the autosave. This moment stays exactly as you leave it — dying does not write over it.</div>
                }
                <div class="save-surface-foot save-surface-foot-center">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-success"
                            title="@(bankKind == BankPromptKind.Edit ? "Write this page onto the berth" : bankKind == BankPromptKind.Export ? "Download this moment as a file carrying this page" : "Bank this moment into the berth with this page on it")"
                            @onclick="CommitBankPrompt">@(bankKind switch { BankPromptKind.Edit => "✎ Write the page", BankPromptKind.Export => "⬇ Export it", _ => "⤓ Bank it" })</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light"
                            title="Change nothing — go back to the logbook"
                            @onclick="CancelBankPrompt">Cancel</button>
                </div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    // ── WHAT THESE PARAMETERS ARE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // #251 item 1 · Every [Parameter] below carries a member of the page under THE MEMBER'S OWN NAME —
    // a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate with its own signature, a variable the
    // page's `@if` binds arrives under the name the `@if` gave it. That is the whole trick of this
    // refactor: it is what let the markup above move out of Map.razor without a single character of it
    // changing, and what lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as they read it
    // when it lived in the page. A parameter that needs saying more than that says it on its own line.

    /// <summary>the page's `string _bankNote` — and this markup WRITES it, so it crosses as a pair: the
    /// value in, the page's own setter out. The private property below keeps the member's own name, so
    /// the moved block still assigns to `_bankNote` and the assignment still lands on the page.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string _bankNoteValue { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>The page's `_bankNote = value`, handed down so the write survives the move.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action<string> _bankNoteSet { get; set; } = default!;
    private string _bankNote { get => _bankNoteValue; set { _bankNoteValue = value; _bankNoteSet(value); } }
    [Parameter] public BankPromptKind? _bankPrompt { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string _bankSlotId { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `string _bankTitle` — and this markup WRITES it, so it crosses as a pair: the
    /// value in, the page's own setter out. The private property below keeps the member's own name, so
    /// the moved block still assigns to `_bankTitle` and the assignment still lands on the page.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string _bankTitleValue { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>The page's `_bankTitle = value`, handed down so the write survives the move.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action<string> _bankTitleSet { get; set; } = default!;
    private string _bankTitle { get => _bankTitleValue; set { _bankTitleValue = value; _bankTitleSet(value); } }
    [Parameter] public string BankPromptHeading { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action CancelBankPrompt { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action CommitBankPrompt { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public BankPromptKind bankKind { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
